// file: vvaharness/agentdoc.py
// Packaged operating instructions for AI coding agents (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md skill, GEMINI.md).
// Written by `vvaharness setup --install-agents`; tells an agent to OPERATE the tool, not edit it.

@executedBy(MODEL) @role(prompt)
class Agentdoc {

    Prompt run() {
        // AGENT_DOC: canonical cross-tool operating manual (Apache header comment first).
        Prompt p = new Prompt();
        p.persona("Operating vvaharness (for AI coding agents): a released CLI SAST product; operate it, do not develop or repair it."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:31
        p.context("Writes a Markdown report and SARIF 2.1.0; findings are triage candidates, not confirmed vulnerabilities."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:34
        p.include(fourRules());
        p.rule("Before scanning: prompts send target source to the model provider and spend tokens; run `vvaharness estimate --repo <path>` first."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:49
        p.include(runIt());
        p.include(onFailure());
        return p;
    }

    Prompt fourRules() {
        Prompt p = new Prompt();
        p.forbid("Never edit the vvaharness package source to make a scan run.");                   // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:38
        p.forbid("Never hand-write config files; use a shipped profile via --config (only exception: git-ignored config.local.yaml)."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:40
        p.must("On any failure run `vvaharness setup` or `doctor`, fix the environment, re-run; report bugs with VVAHARNESS_DEBUG=1."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:42
        p.must("Scan only code the user is authorized to scan; never arm exploit verification or fix mode unless the user asks."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:45
        return p;
    }

    Prompt runIt() {
        Prompt p = new Prompt();
        p.step(1, "pipx install . ; vvaharness setup ; vvaharness scan --repo <path> --stop-after s9");  // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:55
        p.choose(List.of("default", "sdk", "full", "taint", "semgrep"));  // profile choice           // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:60
        p.context("Packaged default sets step_remediate.enabled=false and step_validate.enabled=false; --remediate enables S10 only and can edit target source."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:65
        p.rule("Keep --stop-after s9 to explicitly skip S10/S11 with any profile.");                 // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:71
        p.rule("Exploit verification is Beta, API only: sends live HTTP attack traffic when EV_API_COLLECTION is set; --resume re-arms it."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:73
        p.rule("To send no traffic, unset EV_API_COLLECTION and start a fresh run without --resume."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:78
        p.rule("Behind a gateway set ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL (and SSL_CERT_FILE for a private CA).");    // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:83
        return p;
    }

    Prompt onFailure() {
        Prompt p = new Prompt();
        p.step(1, "Read the one-line scan-failed message, run `vvaharness doctor`, fix what it flags, re-run."); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:88
        return p;
    }

    Prompt claudeSkill() {
        // CLAUDE_SKILL: frontmatter (name: vvaharness, description) + AGENT_DOC
        Prompt p = new Prompt();
        p.format("frontmatter name: vvaharness; description: operate the CLI, never edit source, EV is Beta and API-only, do not arm unless asked"); // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:96
        p.include(run());                                                                           // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:102
        return p;
    }

    Prompt geminiDoc() {
        return run().retitled("(for the Gemini CLI)");                                             // src: vvaharness/agentdoc.py:106
    }
}
